# Drafted by Gemini (side quests batch 1: feast), edited.

~ holly_start
holly_aster [angry]: Listen close, newcomers. Tomorrow is the Founders' feast, and Siv Harga thinks her greasy sausage rolls belong at the high table over my spiced harvest loaf.
holly_aster [sly]: Take this warm loaf to Mayor Somerton and praise my crust. Sneak a bite of Siv's pastry first, and tell me if her suet beats my cinnamon.
* We will help -> holly_accept
* Not now -> END

~ holly_accept
holly_aster [smile]: Bless your honest tongues. Mind you hold the cloth flat so the glaze stays shiny.
quest bread_and_circuses asked
set feast_asked
-> END

~ siv_visit
siv_harga [angry]: Holly Aster sent you sniffing round my block? That woman bakes dry sawdust and calls it sacred custom.
siv_harga [neutral]: Try a pork roll first, fresh from the tin. Better yet, take a tray to Mayor Somerton and tell him real meat beats sweet dough.
* Taste a sausage roll -> taste
* Carry a roll to the mayor too -> siv_accept
* Leave -> END

~ taste
Narrator: The pastry flakes at first bite, rich with sage, black pepper, and clean pork fat. It is remarkably good.
siv_harga [smile]: Ha! Your eyes just went wide as saucers, stranger. Tell Holly that when you see her.
set siv_tasted
-> siv_visit

~ siv_accept
siv_harga [smile]: Good on you. Keep the grease paper wrapped tight till you reach Somerton's parlour.
set siv_roll_carried
-> END

~ mayor_judges
wendel_somerton [smile]: Come in, come in, my dear friends! Have you brought the contenders for tomorrow's high table?
Narrator: The mayor samples the spiced crust and warm pastry, wiping his chin with a linen napkin.
wendel_somerton [weary]: Both are splendid, yet tradition demands a single crown dish. Which baker claims your vote?
* Praise Holly's loaf -> praise_holly
* Praise Siv's rolls -> praise_siv
* [Persuasion DC 13] Suggest both be served -> both_ok | both_fail
* Poison Siv's table with a pinch of salt -> sabotage

~ praise_holly
wendel_somerton [smile]: The spiced loaf it is! Sweet grain and dark clove, just as the Old Ways remember.
set feast_winner = "holly"
standing old_ways +1
-> ode

~ praise_siv
wendel_somerton [smile]: The sausage rolls take the honour! Hearty fare from the Patient Lady's pasture.
set feast_winner = "siv"
standing patient_lady +1
-> ode

~ both_ok
wendel_somerton [smile]: By the Oak, what wisdom! Savory meat in the left hand, sweet bread in the right! A toast to harmony!
set feast_winner = "both"
standing old_ways +1
standing patient_lady +1
-> ode

~ both_fail
wendel_somerton [sad]: Alas, the Founders' charter allows only one dish to lead the grace. You must choose between them.
-> mayor_judges

~ sabotage
Narrator: While the mayor fetches his goblet, {name} tips coarse salt straight into Siv's gravy seam. She will never know who ruined the batch.
wendel_somerton [afraid]: Merciful heavens, this meat is brined like an old boot! Holly's spiced loaf wins by default!
set feast_winner = "holly"
set feast_sabotaged
standing patient_lady -1
-> ode

~ ode
Narrator: Lanterns swing above the trestle tables as Ambrose Quill rises and clears his throat.
ambrose_quill [smile]: O blessed feast of Wickermoor, where crumbs fall down to sweep the floor! May bad meat never make us sicker, nor empty tankards drain the quicker!
Narrator: Dead silence hangs over the taproom for three heartbeats, followed by polite, bewildered clapping.
quest bread_and_circuses done
set feast_done
gold +30
-> END
